@startuml ASignX_System_Architecture
title ASignX - Proposed System Architecture
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #526581
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EDF3FF
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FAFCFF

actor "Guest" as Guest
actor "Registered Learner" as Learner
actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "ML Developer" as MLDev

node "User Device / Web Browser" {
  component "ASignX Web Application\nReact + Vite" as Web
  component "ASignLive\nLive recognition and text output" as Live
  component "ASign Learn\nCourses, lessons, quizzes, practice" as Learn
  component "Sign Strike Arcade\nAlphabet and fingerspelling game" as Arcade
  component "Profile and Progress\nCompleted lessons, XP, streaks, badges" as Progress
  component "Administration Interface\nManage learning content" as AdminUI
  component "Camera Capture\nBrowser MediaDevices API" as Camera
  component "Landmark Extraction and\nTemporal Sequence Buffer" as Features <<proposed>>
  component "Prediction Feedback\nLabel, confidence, stability filtering" as Feedback <<proposed>>
}

node "Application Server\nNode.js + Express + TypeScript" {
  component "REST API\nRequest validation, token verification,\nrole and ownership checks" as API
  component "Learning and Content Logic\nEnrollment, quizzes, lesson completion" as LearningAPI
  component "Progress Logic\nValidated XP awards, streaks, achievements" as ProgressAPI
  component "Recognition History Logic\nOpt-in Live results and practice attempts" as HistoryAPI
  component "Drizzle ORM" as ORM
}

node "Recognition Service (Proposed)\nRuntime and model framework to be selected" {
  component "Inference Endpoint\nValidate landmark sequences" as Inference
  component "ASL Recognition Model\nStatic signs and movement sequences" as Model
}

cloud "Supabase" {
  component "Supabase Auth\nIdentity and access tokens" as Auth
  database "PostgreSQL\n16 proposed application tables" as DB
  storage "Supabase Storage\nCurated sign demonstrations\nand versioned model artifacts" as Storage
}

package "Offline Model Development" {
  artifact "ASL Datasets\nStatic and movement examples" as Dataset
  component "Preprocessing, Training\nand Evaluation" as Training
}

Guest --> Web : Explore / use transient Live
Learner --> Web : Learn / practice / track progress
Admin --> Web : Manage published content
Web --> Live
Web --> Learn
Web --> Progress
Web --> AdminUI
Learn --> Arcade
Live --> Camera
Learn --> Camera : Camera practice
Arcade --> Camera : Sign input
Camera --> Features : Transient frames
Features --> Inference : Landmark sequences\nproposed secure inference connection
Inference --> Model : Predict
Model --> Inference : Sign label + confidence\n+ model version
Inference --> Feedback : Prediction response
Feedback --> Live : Build recognized text
Feedback --> Learn : Practice feedback
Feedback --> Arcade : Match fingerspelled targets

Web --> Auth : Register / sign in / refresh
Auth --> Web : Access token
Web --> API : HTTPS / JSON + access token\npublic routes allow guests
API --> Auth : Verify issued tokens
API --> LearningAPI
API --> ProgressAPI
API --> HistoryAPI
LearningAPI --> ORM
ProgressAPI --> ORM
HistoryAPI --> ORM
ORM --> DB : SQL over TLS
Auth --> DB : Managed auth.users identity
API --> Storage : Authorized media management
Web --> Storage : Read permitted demonstration media
Storage --> Model : Load approved model artifact

MLDev --> Training : Develop and evaluate model
Dataset --> Training
Training --> Storage : Publish versioned artifact
MLDev --> DB : Controlled registration of model metadata

note bottom of Features
  Design assumption: extract landmarks in the browser
  and run recognition in a separate model service.
  Confirm deployment placement before implementation.
end note

note bottom of DB
  Identity: profiles (linked to auth.users)
  Content: signs, courses, lessons, lesson_signs,
    exercises, exercise_options
  Learning: enrollments, lesson_progress, exercise_attempts,
    practice_attempts
  Recognition: model_versions, recognition_sessions,
    recognition_results
  Rewards: achievements, user_achievements
end note

note bottom of HistoryAPI
  Save Live history only for authenticated users who opt in.
  Guest and unsaved Live sessions remain transient.
  Do not persist camera frames or raw video.
end note

note bottom of Arcade
  Arcade scores remain separate from lesson XP.
  Persistent arcade results are outside the current schema.
end note

legend bottom
  This is the intended architecture, not the current implementation.
  Current app: React UI, local camera preview, browser-saved progress,
  simulated recognition/game input, demo accounts, basic Express server.
  The 16-table schema, authentication integration, business APIs,
  recognition service and model integration remain proposed.
  ML Developer is an operational actor, not an application role.
endlegend
@enduml
